  "id": "Compound::DB00402 - Gene::2554",
  "verbalization": "Eszopiclone, a central nervous system depressant, is linked to Gabra1 through a series of molecular and functional interactions. The evidence suggests that Eszopiclone binds to Gabra4, which then participates in Gaba receptor activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Gabra1, indicating a potential role in the regulation of GABAergic signaling. The varying scores in the paths reflect the strength of the relationships, with Eszopiclone binding to Gabra4 in all three paths, and Gabra4 participating in Gaba receptor activity in two of them. The presence of Gabra1 as a downstream participant in Gaba receptor activity suggests that Eszopiclone may influence GABAergic signaling through Gabra4, potentially modulating neuronal excitation. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Eszopiclone interacts with the GABA system, though the exact functional role of Gabra1 in this context remains to be fully elucidated.",
